 ### Euler Integration
-A first-order vector field integrator that computes the next step using only the current position and vector field value ($x_{n+1} = x_n + dt \cdot v(x_n)$). It has a local error of $O(dt^2)$ and is significantly faster but less accurate than RK4. It is suitable for quick previews or when computational resources are extremely limited, but it tends to escape vortices and accumulates error quickly [S1, unofficial].
